{
  "id": "efa8b593-95ce-5763-8cc3-dbff433a1f0a",
  "quality_score": 0.92,
  "review_status": "auto-approved",
  "content_json": {
    "id": "tr-b2-compound-evidential-rivayet",
    "cefr": "B2",
    "title": "Compound evidential \"rivayet\" — copula -(y)mIş on all tenses",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "what-is-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Turkish marks the source of information grammatically. The suffix "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-(y)mIş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " is the evidential copula — the reported-speech or inferential form of the verb «to be». At A2 you met the finite past "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-mIş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " on its own (e.g. "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "gelmiş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " — «he has apparently come»). At B2 the same copula attaches to "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "other tense suffixes"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " — present continuous, aorist/habitual, future, and necessity — to signal that the speaker did not witness the situation directly but is reporting it from hearsay, reading, or inference. This compound form is traditionally called "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "rivayet birleşik zamanı"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " (the «reported compound tense»). It is tense-neutral in the sense that the tense itself is carried by the inner suffix; -(y)mIş only adds the evidential layer on top."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "what is it?"
      },
      {
        "id": "when-to-use-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Use the compound evidential whenever you want to report or infer something about a situation that is framed in a tense other than the simple past. The four main trigger conditions are:"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Hearsay about an ongoing situation."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " You heard or read that something is happening right now or habitually. Use "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "hilite",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-Iyormuş"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " for present continuous or "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "hilite",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-ArmIş / -IrmIş"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " for habitual/aorist."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Reported future plans or predictions."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Someone told you that something will happen. Use "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "hilite",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-AcAkmIş"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Reported obligation or necessity."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " You are relaying someone else's judgment about what must be done. Use "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "hilite",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "-mAlIymIş"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Inference from evidence."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Even without a second-hand source, if you are drawing a conclusion from indirect evidence (e.g. tracks in the snow, a note left behind), the same forms apply."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "variant": "warn",
            "children": [
              {
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "The compound evidential cannot be built on the simple past suffix "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "hilite",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "-DI"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": ". For reported past events use the finite "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "hilite",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "-mIş"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " alone (e.g. "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "em",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "gelmiş"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": ", not "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "em",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "*geldimiş"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": ")."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "when to use it?"
      },
      {
        "id": "formation",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The structure is always: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "verb stem + tense suffix + -(y)mIş + person ending (group 2)"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ". The connecting glide "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-y-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " appears only when the tense suffix ends in a vowel (e.g. aorist "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-Ar/-Ir"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " → "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-ArmIş, -IrmIş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "; future "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-AcAk"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " → "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-AcAkmIş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " — no glide needed because the tense suffix ends in a consonant). Person endings after -(y)mIş are the "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "group-2 (possessive-type)"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " endings, not the group-1 verb endings."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Group-2 person endings used after -(y)mIş:"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "head": [
              "person",
              "ending",
              "example (geliyormuş-)"
            ],
            "kind": "conjugation-table",
            "rows": [
              [
                "1st sg.",
                "-(y)Im",
                "geliyormuşum"
              ],
              [
                "2nd sg.",
                "-sIn",
                "geliyormuşsun"
              ],
              [
                "3rd sg.",
                "—",
                "geliyormuş"
              ],
              [
                "1st pl.",
                "-(y)Iz",
                "geliyormuşuz"
              ],
              [
                "2nd pl.",
                "-sInIz",
                "geliyormuşsunuz"
              ],
              [
                "3rd pl.",
                "-lAr",
                "geliyormuşlar"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "The table below shows the four compound evidential tenses built on the verb "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "çalış-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " («to work») in the 3rd person singular, which has no overt ending:"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "head": [
              "tense",
              "suffix sequence",
              "3rd sg. form",
              "meaning"
            ],
            "kind": "conjugation-table",
            "rows": [
              [
                "present continuous",
                "-Iyor + muş",
                "çalışıyormuş",
                "apparently he/she is working"
              ],
              [
                "aorist / habitual",
                "-Ir + mIş",
                "çalışırmış",
                "apparently he/she works (habitually)"
              ],
              [
                "future",
                "-AcAk + mIş",
                "çalışacakmış",
                "apparently he/she will work"
              ],
              [
                "necessity",
                "-mAlI + ymIş",
                "çalışmalıymış",
                "apparently he/she must work"
              ]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "formation"
      },
      {
        "id": "examples-in-context",
        "body": [
          {
            "en": "Apparently Ahmet knows German very well.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Present continuous + evidential copula: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "bil-iyor-muş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ". The speaker learned this from someone else, not by direct observation."
              }
            ],
            "target": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Ahmet çok iyi Almanca "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "biliyormuş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "They say they used to live here.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Aorist/habitual + evidential copula: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "otur-ur-lar-mış"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ". The 3rd plural aorist "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-lAr"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " precedes the copula here, as is standard for 3rd plural aorist evidential."
              }
            ],
            "target": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Eskiden burada "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "otururlarmış"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "en": "Supposedly he will come tomorrow.",
            "kind": "example",
            "note": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Future + evidential copula: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "mono",
                "children": [
                  {
